  "term": "olfactory mucosa",
  "definition": "The olfactory mucosa is the part of the nasal lining at the top of each nasal cavity that contains the sensory nerve endings used for smell. Its specialized olfactory epithelium includes receptor neurons, brush cells, stem cells, and related olfactory glands.",
